  "identityStatus": "Native building way 53263911 and native heritage identifier Q337871. The perimeter includes the stepped masonry and apsidal buttresses. Photographs set the roof hierarchy and the city gives the exact restored tower height.",
  "terrainContact": {
    "local": [
      7,
      39.3
    ],
    "modelY": 0,
    "basis": "Sampled the original open elevation field at the western tower approach; the footprint’s stone footing follows the sloping site."
  },
  "notes": "Szczecin’s city heritage account documents the 110.18 m restored spire. Rüdiger Schlott’s post-restoration photo and Kapitel’s exact crown detail show the retained Gothic tower, analog dials, copper-toned spire and four corner pinnacles. Horvat’s earlier clear view supports only the standing choir and the broad green nave roof."
}
